Folio reads SQLite session stores written by OpenCode. OpenCode is an
independent project distributed under the MIT License
(https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode). Folio is not affiliated with or
endorsed by the OpenCode project.

Storage layouts, JSON message shapes, ordering rules and the v1-to-v2 migration
completion marker were verified against these pinned upstream revisions before
implementation. They are referenced as behavioral specifications only:

- OpenCode v1.18.34, commit aec0b9a6d8898f68f923aaf08b7306d931fd9d76
  (session / message / part tables, message-created+id ordering, native part IDs,
  synthetic/ignored/summary flags, tool state fields).
- OpenCode v2.0.21, commit 8a8bd622a3d7dc29ccf30ec17f84e363ed95ed72
  (session_v2 / session_message tables, seq ordering, scalar user.text and
  assistant content item shapes, tool/file/error content shapes, and the
  migration.v1-v2 KV marker with {phase:"completed"}).

The design contract lives in the private O3P workspace; this repository ships
only original implementation code, synthetic test fixtures and project
licensing.

Runtime dependencies: none beyond the Node.js standard library (node:sqlite,
node:fs, node:path, node:util, node:crypto). Build-time devDependencies
(TypeScript, @types/node) are MIT/Apache-2.0 licensed and are not redistributed
in the published package contents beyond normal npm dependency metadata.
